## Baseline Model
The original LSTM model follows the official Keras time-series forecasting example using the Jena Climate dataset. It uses:
A single LSTM layer
Fixed sequence length (historical window)
Default batch size and learning rate
Basic preprocessing and scaling
One-step forecasting output

## Increased Model Depth (Stacked LSTM)
Modified from single LSTM → multiple LSTM layers
Allows the model to learn:
Low-level temporal patterns (first layer)
Higher-level trends (deeper layers)
Impact:
Better ability to capture long-term dependencies
Improved forecasting stability for complex weather patterns

